<h3>What is PTSD?</h3>
<p>Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder (PTSD) is a mental health condition triggered by experiencing or witnessing a traumatic event. Trauma can stem from:</p>
<ul>
<li>Abuse (childhood, emotional, sexual, physical)</li>
<li>Military combat</li>
<li>Accidents or natural disasters</li>
<li>Violence or crime</li>
<li>Medical trauma or unexpected loss</li>
</ul>
<p>Not everyone who experiences trauma develops PTSD, but when symptoms persist, professional treatment can make a significant difference.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="dm-service-section">
<div class="dm-container">
<div class="dm-flex">
<div class="dm-full">
<h3>Symptoms of PTSD and Trauma</h3>
<ul>
<li>Flashbacks, nightmares, or intrusive thoughts</li>
<li>Avoidance of people, places, or memories</li>
<li>Heightened startle response or hypervigilance</li>
<li>Emotional numbness or detachment</li>
<li>Irritability, anger, or outbursts</li>
<li>Difficulty sleeping or concentrating</li>
<li>Feelings of guilt, shame, or hopelessness</li>
</ul>
<p>Untreated trauma can also lead to depression, anxiety, and chronic relationship problems.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
